# Known-flaky / non-checkable external links (regexes, anchored).
# Lychee treats every line as an unanchored regex, so each entry must be
# escaped + anchored to match only the intended URLs (a bare prefix like
# `https://example.com/*` would match every https:// URL as a regex).
# Storefronts often bot-block CI runners; localhost URLs are dev-only.
^https://apps\.apple\.com/.*$
^https://play\.google\.com/.*$
^http://localhost.*$
^https://t\.co/.*$
# Placeholder / example URLs in docs.
^https://example\.com/.*$
^https://presigned\.example/.*$
^https://<
^https://\.\.\.
# Auth-walled or retired third-party endpoints referenced in docs.
^https://dashboard\.stripe\.com/.*$
^https://generativelanguage\.googleapis\.com/.*$
^https://apihub\.agnes-ai\.com/.*$
^https://storage\.railway\.app.*$
